### [@mastra/libsql@1.29.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/libsql@1.29.0/stores/libsql/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Changes to an experimental, upcoming memory feature. (#28353)

  The Knowledge storage domain now stores Knowledge as pages, notes and pins (schema 4) instead of nodes and records. On startup, the tables of the earlier experimental Knowledge node store (shipped in 1.79.0) are dropped, with any rows in them, and the new tables are created; this also happens if an older process recreates them during a rolling deploy. Memory and other tables are never touched. On MongoDB, Knowledge collections found without a schema version (for example, left by an interrupted first start) are adopted as schema 4 rather than refused. Don't run `dangerouslyReset()` from an older version against a database the new version already uses. Knowledge pages need a `@mastra/core` release that includes them; with an older core, the other storage domains keep working.

  _Also in: @mastra/mongodb@1.26.0, @mastra/mysql@0.16.0, @mastra/pg@1.35.0_

- Store Knowledge listing pins. The pins table gets a `kind` column (`page` or `list`) and a `depth` column, and a page now holds one pin per kind. Existing pins become page pins; no reset is needed. (#29263)

  **Migration step on first start.** Each store upgrades its pins table once, the first time it starts with this version:

  - LibSQL rebuilds the pins table (SQLite can't drop the old one-pin-per-page constraint in place): it creates the new table, copies every pin across as a page pin, and swaps it in, inside the init transaction.
  - Postgres and MySQL alter the table in place (add `kind` and `depth`, replace the unique key on the page with one on page and kind).
  - MongoDB sets `kind: 'page'` on existing pins and replaces the unique index on `pageId` with one on `pageId` and `kind`.

  _Also in: @mastra/mongodb@1.26.0, @mastra/mysql@0.16.0, @mastra/pg@1.35.0_

#### Patch Changes

- Database-backed agents now retain Editor changes to static model fallback lists across restarts, and existing LibSQL and PostgreSQL databases upgrade automatically. (#27287)

  _Also in: @mastra/mongodb@1.26.0, @mastra/pg@1.35.0_

- Knowledge stores can list and count only the child scopes a reader can see, so `knowledge_list` no longer reads every child scope to show the readable ones. (#29260)

  _Also in: @mastra/mongodb@1.26.0, @mastra/mysql@0.16.0, @mastra/pg@1.35.0_

- The LibSQL Knowledge store keeps the page link index: a `mastra_knowledge_page_links` table, created on startup in existing databases without a schema change. (#29260)


### [@mastra/mcp@2.8.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/mcp@2.8.0/packages/mcp/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Added an `onServerSettled` option to `listToolsWithErrors()`, `listToolsetsWithErrors()`, and `listToolDefinitionsWithErrors()`. It is called for each server as soon as that server's discovery succeeds, fails, or times out, so you can show healthy servers right away instead of waiting for the slowest one. (#29028)

  A server that hits `perServerTimeoutMs` now reports an error with `code: MCP_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT_CODE` (exported from `@mastra/mcp`), so you can tell a slow server apart from one that failed.

  Added a `serverNames` option to the same methods to discover only the named servers. Use it to retry the servers that timed out without starting every other server again.

  The `onServerSettled` callback may be `async`. If it throws or rejects, the error is logged and discovery is unaffected — a rejected callback never surfaces as an unhandled rejection.

  ```ts
  await mcp.listToolsetsWithErrors({
    perServerTimeoutMs: 60_000,
    onServerSettled: (serverName, { value, error, duration }) => {
      console.log(serverName, error ? error.message : Object.keys(value), duration);
    },
  });
  ```

- Added a `toolResult` option to `MCPServer` so tools can return images, audio, and files to MCP clients. (#29247)

  Set `toolResult.modelOutput: true` to build each result from the tool's `toModelOutput`, the same output an agent sends to its model. Images become `image` blocks, audio becomes `audio` blocks, and other files become embedded resources. For example, a workspace `read_file` of a PNG now reaches the client as an image instead of base64 inside JSON text.

  ```ts
  const server = new MCPServer({
    id: 'media-server',
    name: 'Media Server',
    version: '1.0.0',
    tools: { screenshotTool },
    toolResult: { modelOutput: true },
  });
  ```

  Use `toolResult.transform` to rewrite any completed tool result before it is sent, for example to forward results that are already MCP-shaped from proxied tools.

  Without the new option, results are unchanged. The default of `modelOutput` becomes `true` in the next major version; if your clients parse the raw JSON text of tools that define `toModelOutput`, set `modelOutput: false` to keep the current behavior.

- Added answering MCP task input from the agent chat. When a tool call that continues as an MCP task needs input, and no `inputRequests` handler is configured, the call now suspends with the server's requests instead of failing with `MCP_CLIENT_TOOL_TASK_INPUT_UNHANDLED`. The remote task stays open. Resuming the call answers that same task, and the tool is never called a second time. (#29032)

  ```typescript
  // The tool call suspended with { type: 'mcp-input-request', taskId, requests: { approve: { ... } } }
  await agent.resumeStream(
    { inputResponses: { approve: { action: 'accept', content: { ok: true } } } },
    { runId, toolCallId },
  );
  ```

  If the server asks again, the call suspends again with a new `requestedAt`, so a UI can tell the new request from the one it already answered. A configured `inputRequests` handler still answers first, and a direct `tool.execute()` call without an agent or workflow still fails as before. See #28986.

#### Patch Changes

- Fixed `MCPServer` denying calls to tools it had just listed when fine-grained authorization is configured. (#29077)

- Fixed `disconnect()` hanging, and stdio server processes being left running, when a server never answered its connection handshake. (#29028)

- Fixed `MCPServer` answering a call to an unknown tool with an `isError: true` tool result. (#29204)


### [@mastra/memory@1.41.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/memory@1.41.0/packages/memory/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Observational Memory semantic search now works with a vector store that generates embeddings itself, so no `embedder` is needed. (#27005)

  With MongoDB Automated Embedding, MongoDB embeds each observation when it is written and the search string when you query:

  ```ts
  const memory = new Memory({
    storage,
    vector: new MongoDBVector({ id: 'vec', uri, dbName, autoEmbed: { model: 'voyage-4' } }),
    options: { observationalMemory: { retrieval: { vector: true } } },
  });

  await memory.searchMessages({ query: 'What deadline did we agree on?', resourceId: 'user-123' });
  ```

  The agent's `recall` tool searches the same way. Observations are indexed under `memory_observations_selfembed`. Configurations that pass an `embedder` keep working unchanged.

#### Patch Changes

- Fixed memory recall exposing stored reasoning. (#28810)

- Fixed Observational Memory context leaving the `<observations>` block open. (#29224)

- Observational Memory now tells the Observer who sent each user signal. (#29176)


