### [@mastra/ring-signals@0.1.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/ring-signals@0.1.0/signals/ring/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Added `@mastra/ring-signals` for connecting Ring doorbells and cameras to Mastra agents. Ring events such as doorbell presses and motion arrive in agent threads as notification signals, and the agent can fetch a snapshot or video clip for an event with the `ring_snapshot` and `ring_clip` tools. (#28864)

  ```ts
  import { Agent } from '@mastra/core/agent';
  import { RingSignals } from '@mastra/ring-signals';

  export const homeAgent = new Agent({
    id: 'home-agent',
    name: 'Home Agent',
    instructions: 'Say briefly whether each doorbell event needs attention.',
    model: 'openai/gpt-6.1-sol',
    signals: [
      new RingSignals({
        events: {
          device_offline: { priority: 'low', summary: 'Device went offline.', coalesce: true },
        },
      }),
    ],
  });
  ```

  Mastra adds the routes Ring calls for account linking and webhooks to the server. See the [Ring integration guide](https://mastra.ai/integrations/channels/ring).

### [@mastra/server@1.82.0](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/@mastra/server@1.82.0/packages/server/CHANGELOG.md)
#### Minor Changes

- Added `POST /api/background-tasks/:backgroundTaskId/resume` to answer a suspended background task over HTTP. (#28998)

  - Send the answer as `resumeData`.
  - Optionally send the `suspendedAt` you read from the task. If the task has resumed or suspended again since then, the server answers `409` instead of delivering a stale answer.
  - Background task responses now include `suspendedAt`.
  - The route needs the new `background-tasks:execute` permission.

  ```bash
  curl -X POST http://localhost:4111/api/background-tasks/$TASK_ID/resume \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d '{"resumeData":{"approved":true},"suspendedAt":"2026-10-30T10:00:00.000Z"}'
  ```

#### Patch Changes

- `server.auth.authorize(path, method, user, context)` can now call `context.get('requestContext')` and `context.get('mastra')` on the Express, Fastify, Koa and Elysia adapters, as it already could on Hono. (#29069)

  _Also in: @mastra/server-adapters-test-suite@0.2.1_

- Fixed agent-builder routes in processes that run more than one Mastra instance. (#29253)

